<title>AUSTRIA: VAI wins order from British Steel.</title>
<headline>VAI wins order from British Steel.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>VAI UK, a unit of Austria's Voest-Alpine Industrieanlagenbau GmbH (VAI), said on Friday it had been awarded a contract by British Steel to modernise the pickling line at its Llanwern works.</p>
<p>The project worth 190 million schillings (10 million sterling) includes the design, supply, installation and commissioning of mechanical, civil and electrical equipment, VAI said in a statement.</p>
<p>VAI UK was set up in the UK in 1996. VAI is fully owned by Austria's technical engineering group VA Technologie AG.</p>
<p>-- Vienna Newsroom, +43 1 531 12 275</p>
